  "body": "In Node.js, a `%j` formatting specifier runs `JSON.stringify()` on the related arg. I am unsure what checks it makes other than `'[Circular]'`, but I can take a look.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```\r\n$ node\r\n> console.log('JSON: %j', { greeting: 'hello!' })\r\nJSON: {\"greeting\":\"hello!\"}\r\n````\r\n\r\nMore information can be found in our docs on [`util.format(format[, ...args])`](https://nodejs.org/dist/latest-v7.x/docs/api/util.html#util_util_format_format_args) (Effectively our equivalent of the spec's Format function.)",
